# DAX Measures Used in Healthcare Patient Analytics Dashboard

This document contains the key DAX measures used to solve business problems related to hospital performance, revenue analysis, patient satisfaction, and readmission analysis.

---

# 1. Total Patients

### Purpose
Calculates the total number of unique patients treated.

```DAX
Total Patients =
DISTINCTCOUNT(Healthcare[PatientID])
```

---

# 2. Total Revenue

### Purpose
Calculates total revenue generated by the hospital.

```DAX
Total Revenue =
SUM(Healthcare[TreatmentCostINR])
```

---

# 3. Average Satisfaction Score

### Purpose
Measures overall patient satisfaction.

```DAX
Avg Satisfaction =
AVERAGE(Healthcare[SatisfactionScore])
```

---

# 4. Average Length of Stay

### Purpose
Calculates the average number of days patients stay in the hospital.

```DAX
Avg Length Of Stay =
AVERAGE(Healthcare[LengthOfStayDays])
```

---

# 5. Readmitted Patients

### Purpose
Counts the number of patients readmitted within 30 days.

```DAX
Readmitted Patients =
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS(Healthcare),
    Healthcare[Readmitted30Days] = "Yes"
)
```

---

# 6. Readmission Rate

### Purpose
Measures the percentage of patients readmitted.

```DAX
Readmission Rate =
DIVIDE(
    [Readmitted Patients],
    [Total Patients]
)
```

---

# 7. Revenue Per Patient

### Purpose
Calculates average revenue generated per patient.

```DAX
Revenue Per Patient =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue],
    [Total Patients]
)
```

---

# 8. Year-To-Date (YTD) Revenue

### Purpose
Calculates cumulative revenue from the beginning of the year.

```DAX
YTD Revenue =
TOTALYTD(
    [Total Revenue],
    Dim_Date[Date]
)
```

---

# 9. Previous Month Revenue

### Purpose
Returns the revenue generated in the previous month.

```DAX
Previous Month Revenue =
CALCULATE(
    [Total Revenue],
    PREVIOUSMONTH(Dim_Date[Date])
)
```

---

# 10. Revenue Growth %

### Purpose
Calculates month-over-month revenue growth.

```DAX
Revenue Growth % =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue] - [Previous Month Revenue],
    [Previous Month Revenue]
)
```

---

# Calculated Column

## Age Group

### Purpose
Categorises patients into age groups for demographic analysis.

```DAX
Age Group =
SWITCH(
    TRUE(),
    Dim_Patient[Age] <= 18, "Children",
    Dim_Patient[Age] <= 40, "Young Adults",
    Dim_Patient[Age] <= 60, "Adults",
    "Senior Citizens"
)
```

---

# Date Table

### Purpose
Creates a dedicated date dimension for time intelligence calculations.

```DAX
Dim_Date =
CALENDAR(
    MIN(Healthcare[AdmissionDate]),
    MAX(Healthcare[AdmissionDate])
)
```

### Additional Date Columns

```DAX
Year =
YEAR(Dim_Date[Date])

Quarter =
"Q" & FORMAT(Dim_Date[Date], "Q")

Month Number =
MONTH(Dim_Date[Date])

Month Name =
FORMAT(Dim_Date[Date], "MMMM")

Week Number =
WEEKNUM(Dim_Date[Date])

Day =
DAY(Dim_Date[Date])
```

